{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f06138ef-84a9-4939-b7e0-f09f88c91992","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9807b9dfdb4f2d7f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-fie5n618/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E001.md","content":"# State-Driven Kueue Workload Status Model for Workbenches\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic reworks how the odh-dashboard derives and displays Kueue workload scheduling status for workbenches. The current status model conflates all Evicted conditions as \"Preempted\" and derives progress from wildcard/substring matching of events. This epic replaces it with a structured, state-driven derivation from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses, distinguishes preemption from other eviction reasons, surfaces requeue/retry state, and renders human-friendly message overrides with a raw-message fallback so a Kueue condition is never shown as a blank state.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Correct the `WorkloadCondition` type union in `k8sTypes.ts`: remove the incorrect `'Failed'` entry (failure is expressed as `Finished` with reason `Failed`) and include `QuotaReserved`, `Admitted`, `PodsReady`, `Finished`, `Evicted`, `Preempted`, `Requeued`, `BlockedOnPreemptionGates`, and `DeactivationTarget`.\n- Build a structured, extensible status derivation model driven by Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses, replacing wildcard/substring matching of events.\n- Distinguish \"Preempted\" (higher-priority workload took resources) from \"Evicted\" (admin action or timeout) and from the full set of eviction reasons: Preempted, PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded.\n- Surface the Requeued state with retry count and next retry time computed from the Workload's `requeueState` (including `requeueAt`).\n- Implement a lookup-table mechanism for human-friendly status message overrides covering known condition/reason combinations, with engineering-authored defaults; the table must be data-driven so reviewed content from the UX/content stream can replace defaults without code rework.\n- Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, and surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n- Always fall back to the raw Kueue condition `.message` field when no override exists — never show a blank state when a Kueue condition exists.\n- Handle Workload CRs containing condition types not yet in the dashboard's type union: show them with raw message text, never silently dropped (backwards compatibility).\n- Keep existing workbench status behavior unchanged when Kueue is not enabled or the workload/namespace is not Kueue-managed (purely additive, conditional changes — this also serves as the rollback safety property).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace where a workbench has been evicted due to `ClusterQueueStopped`, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays \"Evicted\" with reason \"Queue stopped by administrator\" — NOT \"Preempted\", measured by the status label text and variant differing from the Preempted state.\n- Given a workbench has been evicted and the Workload CR has a `Requeued` condition with `requeueState.requeueAt` set, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays retry information including next retry time and attempt count, measured by the status text including the computed retry time from `requeueState`.\n- Given a workbench's Workload CR has a condition type or reason not recognized by the status model, when the workbench status is rendered, then the raw Kueue condition message is displayed rather than a blank state, measured by the status text containing the Workload CR's condition `.message` field content.\n- Given a workload with no Kueue management (no queue label) or a namespace without Kueue management, when the workbench status is rendered, then the status behavior is identical to the pre-change dashboard, measured by unchanged status output on a non-Kueue workbench fixture.\n- Given a Workload CR carrying a condition type outside the dashboard's type union, when the status is rendered, then the condition is displayed with its raw message text, measured by the absence of dropped/silent conditions in the rendered status.\n- Given a workload transitioning between AdmissionCheck pending and retry states, and between WaitForRecovery and WaitForStart, when the status is rendered, then the states are distinguishable, measured by differing status text for each state.\n- Given the human-friendly override table, when reviewed microcopy is delivered by the UX/content stream, then defaults can be replaced without changing derivation logic, measured by the override content being data (lookup table) rather than inline conditionals.\n- Given the full set of known eviction reasons enumerated above, when each is rendered, then Preempted is visually and textually distinct from every other eviction reason, measured by per-reason status label/variant checks.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons (ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, PodsReadyTimeout, Deactivated, etc.) in the workbench status display.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState` when a workload is evicted and waiting to re-enter the queue.\n- HLR-5 [P0]: Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback.\n- HLR-10 [P2]: Improve status model progress steps to ensure all workload scheduling information is surfaced — move away from wildcard/substring matching of events to a structured, extensible status derivation model.\n- HLR-11 [P2]: Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43978,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d10b42d925a884","agent_id":"a34ff37c9054c3317","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"2cfa78c4-bd89-4f79-9a1f-0ba37003ff13","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:05:58.416Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
