{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-44e85297-04e9-40e6-aaad-60e1b08266a8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0d56f50bbbaeb6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-fie5n618/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E002.md","content":"# Kueue Management Indicators: Project Indicator and Workload Anomaly Indicator\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic adds two complementary UI indicators to the odh-dashboard that tell users whether their project and workbenches are managed by Kueue queue-based scheduling: a positive indicator on the project details page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, and an anomaly indicator on individual workloads that are NOT managed by Kueue despite living in a Kueue-managed namespace. Users must know their project uses queue-based scheduling because it fundamentally affects how their workloads start.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a positive Kueue indicator to the project details page, shown when the namespace carries the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label. The exact visual form (info banner, badge, or label) is a UX decision tracked as RHOAIUX-7470; implement an interim visual treatment so development is not blocked, structured so the finalized design can be applied without rework.\n- Add an anomaly indicator on workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label — e.g. created via GitOps or CLI bypassing the dashboard). Do NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every workload in a Kueue-managed namespace — only flag the anomaly.\n- Both indicators must be conditional on namespace/workload labels only; no new backend services or API changes.\n- Indicator logic must not block workload creation or any dashboard workflow (read-only visibility).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists and absent when it does not.\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n- Given a namespace that is not Kueue-managed, when the user views the workbenches overview, then no workload shows the anomaly indicator regardless of queue labels, measured by the indicator being absent on all workloads in non-managed namespaces.\n- Given the interim visual treatment, when the finalized design arrives from the UX stream (RHOAIUX-7470), then the treatment can be swapped without changing the indicator conditions or data plumbing, measured by the indicator presentation being isolated from its label-driven logic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 [P0]: Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n- HLR-4 [P0]: Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45338,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d10b42d925a884","agent_id":"a34ff37c9054c3317","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"3a67e1d9-352b-42e2-81e6-6162873180c2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:06:10.231Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
