{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c0057924-e613-4341-ab7a-06a33cda8c98","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-996c94503088510e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-fie5n618/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E003.md","content":"# Kueue Visibility API Integration for Queue Position Display\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic integrates Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io`) into the odh-dashboard so users can see a pending workbench's position in its queue. Queue position is not a field on the Workload object; it lives on the `PendingWorkload` type served by the Visibility API as subresources on queues. The integration must degrade gracefully when the user's RBAC does not permit reading position data.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a frontend API client for the LocalQueue pending-workloads subresource: `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`, called through the existing `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy with the logged-in user's token (subject to the user's RBAC).\n- Display queue position (`positionInLocalQueue`) for workbenches in a pending/queuing state in the workbenches overview.\n- Handle 403 responses silently using the existing `getGenericErrorCode` pattern from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx` — position info is supplementary, not critical; no error is surfaced to the user.\n- Map pending workloads to notebooks using the existing `buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()` mechanism in `api/k8s/workloads.ts` (`kueue.x-k8s.io/job-name` label match, then ownerReferences matching).\n- Validate whether `batch-user` RBAC (aggregating Kueue's `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`) is present by default in RHOAI clusters, and document the finding — this determines whether position display reaches regular users or is effectively admin-only, but does not change the implementation.\n- No ClusterQueue-level position display (cluster-scoped endpoint is admin-only) and no estimated wait-time predictions — only factual position data.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has `batch-user` RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is displayed (position in local queue), measured by the position number being present and matching the value from the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT have RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is silently omitted with no error displayed, measured by the absence of both position data and error indicators.\n- Given the default RBAC aggregation assumption, when validation completes, then the presence or absence of `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` aggregation for standard users in RHOAI clusters is documented, measured by a recorded finding in the epic's completion notes.\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace with no pending workloads, when the overview renders, then no position information is displayed and no request errors surface, measured by the position element being absent for admitted/running workbenches.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 [P1]: Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display (`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on LocalQueue — gracefully degrade on 403.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46180,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d10b42d925a884","agent_id":"a34ff37c9054c3317","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"31dfa8da-2413-4607-b935-0533e951eb12","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:06:22.500Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into ep