{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-adc3d13e-0ee0-4c8b-b6df-595e7b942964","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a772dff8ff6750c4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-fie5n618/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E004.md","content":"# HardwareProfile Queue UX: GitOps Popover Fallback, LocalQueue Validation, and Dropdown Explanation\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic hardens the HardwareProfile (HP) surfaces in the odh-dashboard for Kueue-managed projects: the HP details popover correctly handles notebooks whose queue label was applied directly via GitOps (no HardwareProfile match), the HP admin form validates LocalQueue names, and the HP dropdown explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n\n## Scope\n\n- HP details popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks: when no HP scheduling data exists for a notebook, fall back to reading the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label from the notebook's own labels; resolve the cluster queue name from the project's LocalQueue list; indicate the source — \"Queue: my-queue (applied directly)\" vs. \"Queue: my-queue (via hardware profile)\". Applying queue labels directly is a supported RHBoK pattern.\n- Add `k8sNameRegex` validation (`/^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$/`) to the LocalQueue name field in the HardwareProfile admin form. Existence of the queue cannot be validated at HP creation time (HardwareProfiles are cluster-scoped, LocalQueues are namespace-scoped, target namespace unknown).\n- At workbench creation time, when the specified LocalQueue does not exist in the target namespace, display a dismissible warning (NOT an error) — the admin may intend the LQ to be created later or via GitOps; Kueue itself reports the error via Workload conditions if the queue truly does not exist.\n- Keep the strict filtering behavior in the HP dropdown (only queue-based HPs shown in Kueue-managed namespaces) and add an explicit info indicator (info icon or tooltip) explaining: \"Only queue-enabled hardware profiles are shown because this project uses queue-based scheduling.\"\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a GitOps-managed workbench with `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label applied directly (no matching HardwareProfile), when the user opens the HardwareProfile details popover, then the popover displays the queue name with indication it was applied directly (not via hardware profile), measured by the popover text including the queue name and a source indicator.\n- Given an admin is creating a HardwareProfile and enters an invalid LocalQueue name (e.g., contains uppercase or spaces), when the form validates, then a validation error is shown for the LocalQueue name field, measured by the form displaying an inline error referencing the Kubernetes name format.\n- Given a workbench is being created with a HardwareProfile referencing a LocalQueue that does not exist in the target namespace, when the creation form is submitted, then a warning (not error) is displayed indicating the local queue was not found, measured by the warning being dismissible and not blocking workbench creation.\n- Given a workbench is in a Kueue-managed namespace and the user opens the workbench creation form, when the HardwareProfile dropdown renders with only queue-enabled profiles, then an info indicator explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown, measured by the presence of a tooltip or info icon adjacent to the dropdown.\n- Given a notebook with a matching HardwareProfile, when the HP details popover renders, then the queue is attributed to the hardware profile (not \"applied directly\"), measured by the source indicator distinguishing the two cases.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 [P1]: Fix HardwareProfile details popover for GitOps-managed notebooks: read queue label directly when no HP match exists, indicate source.\n- HLR-8 [P1]: Add `k8sNameRegex` validation to LocalQueue name field in HardwareProfile admin form.\n- HLR-9 [P1]: Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47049,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d10b42d925a884","agent_id":"a34ff37c9054c3317","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"c03cb86e-0101-4948-a40c-b3658058e899","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:06:35.284Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
