mpletes, then a finalized visual treatment specification is delivered for the positive Kueue indicator, measured by a design deliverable naming the chosen form (banner/badge/label) with usage guidance.\n- Given the anomaly indicator requirement, when design work completes, then a visual treatment specification is delivered for the non-Kueue workload indicator, measured by a design deliverable defining the indicator's appearance and placement in the workbenches overview.\n- Given the engineering defaults for status message overrides, when content review completes, then reviewed/finalized wording decisions are recorded for the known condition/reason combinations, measured by sign-off recorded against RHOAIUX-7470.\n- Given the parallel engineering implementation using placeholders, when the finalized designs are delivered, then they are applicable without structural rework, measured by handoff artifacts referencing the implemented indicator elements and override table structure.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Supporting stream (no HLR ownership): enables the finalized visual treatment for HLR-3 (positive Kueue indicator on project details page) and HLR-4 (anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads), and the content review behind the HLR-5 message overrides. Engineering implementations of those HLRs are not blocked on this epic — placeholder treatment and default copy are used until deliverables land.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48036,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d10b42d925a884","agent_id":"a34ff37c9054c3317","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"8ca54f99-9d5c-4c47-8432-e52d7feca998","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:06:46.852Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
