ia\n\n- Given the enumerated set of known Kueue condition/reason combinations, when the content work completes, then every combination has reviewed human-readable copy, measured by a complete lookup table with one entry per known combination.\n- Given a user without Kubernetes knowledge, when an override message is displayed, then the message explains the state in plain language without requiring Kueue concepts, measured by content review sign-off under RHOAIUX-7470.\n- Given a condition/reason combination not covered by the table, when the dashboard renders it, then the raw Kueue condition message still displays, measured by the copy deliverable not altering the raw-message fallback behavior.\n- Given the dashboard's data-driven override mechanism, when the reviewed copy is delivered, then it can be loaded without code changes, measured by the deliverable matching the lookup-table format the status model implementation consumes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-11 [P2] (wording deliverable): Improve status message granularity — distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states. The engineering state derivation for this HLR lives in the status model implementation; this epic owns the wording.\n- Supporting stream for HLR-5 [P0]: human-friendly message overrides for workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions (engineering defaults are replaced by this epic's reviewed copy).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48807,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81d10b42d925a884","agent_id":"a34ff37c9054c3317","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"1e693d34-2bbd-4b5f-babb-4cded95f3c19","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:06:58.220Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
