{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88ed4d66fc1c6eb6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8002 — Integrate Kueue Workload Scheduling Information in Workbenches Overview\n11\t\n12\t## Decomposition Approach\n13\t\n14\tThe Staff Engineer Input takes precedence over the AI-generated strategy sections. Key inputs applied:\n15\t\n16\t- **Component scope**: Only `odh-dashboard` (frontend) is affected. The rhods-operator HardwareProfile mutating webhook that injects the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label is explicitly out of this strategy's scope (Staff input override — the AI TL;DR's mention of rhods-operator-injected behavior is context only).\n17\t- **Scope constraints override the pre-refinement \"Proposed Solution\" section**: quota/capacity preview (LocalQueues carry no quota), estimated wait-time predictions, rich \"Kueue Insights\" admin visualization, feature-flag model changes, and opt-in/opt-out controls are all out of scope. Only the eleven committed HLRs are decomposed.\n18\t- **Non-blocking UX dependency**: Development must not block on RHOAIUX-7470 (visual treatment and content review). Engineering ships placeholder visual treatment and default message copy; UXD and Content streams run in parallel and their deliverables replace placeholders when ready.\n19\t\n20\t**Component name mapping (canonical list)**: The canonical RHAI component list has no `odh-dashboard` entry; the closest canonical name is `AI Core Dashboard`, used for all dashboard-code and dashboard-content epics. The UXD design epic uses the canonical `UXD` component; the documentation epic uses `Documentation`.\n21\t\n22\t**No Investigation epics.** Both open questions were evaluated against the decision rule (does the answer change which downstream epics exist or what they do?):\n23\t- *Visibility API RBAC aggregation* (`batch-user`/`view`/`edit` aggregating `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`): the implementation is identical either way — display position when authorized, silently omit on 403. Reclassified as a validation acceptance criterion on the Visibility API epic.\n24\t- *Form of the positive Kueue indicator* (banner vs. badge vs. label): the strategy mandates placeholder-driven development with minimal engineering effort regardless of choice. Reclassified as the UXD design epic's deliverable plus an interim-treatment acceptance criterion on the indicator epic.\n25\t\n26\t## Epic List\n27\t\n28\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n29\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E001 | State-driven Kueue workload status model (eviction reasons, requeue state, message overrides) | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E002 | Kueue management indicators (positive project indicator, non-Kueue workload anomaly indicator) | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E003 | Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E004 | HardwareProfile queue UX (GitOps popover fallback, LocalQueue name validation, dropdown filtering explanation) | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E005 | UX design and content review for Kueue visibility indicators (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | UXD | P1 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E006 | Status message microcopy overrides for Kueue workload conditions | Implementation | Content | P1 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E007 | Documentation: release note and feature-docs determination for Kueue workbench visibility | Implementation | Docs | P1 |\n37\t\n38\t## Dependency DAG\n39\t\n40\t```mermaid\n41\tgraph TD\n42\t    E001[\"E001 Status model (P0)\"] --> E007[\"E007 Documentation (P1)\"]\n43\t    E002[\"E002 Kueue indicators (P0)