-|---------------------------|---------|\n72\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons in workbench status | E001 |\n73\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState` | E001 |\n74\t| HLR-3 | P0 | Positive Kueue indicator on project details page (`kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`) | E002 |\n75\t| HLR-4 | P0 | Anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces | E002 |\n76\t| HLR-5 | P0 | Workload scheduling status from Workload CR conditions, human-friendly overrides + raw fallback | E001 |\n77\t| HLR-6 | P1 | Kueue Visibility API queue position (`PendingWorkloadsSummary` on LocalQueue), graceful 403 degradation | E003 |\n78\t| HLR-7 | P1 | HardwareProfile popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks (direct queue label, source indication) | E004 |\n79\t| HLR-8 | P1 | `k8sNameRegex` validation on LocalQueue name field in HardwareProfile admin form | E004 |\n80\t| HLR-9 | P1 | Info indicator on HP dropdown explaining queue-enabled filtering | E004 |\n81\t| HLR-10 | P2 | Structured, extensible status derivation model (away from wildcard/substring event matching) | E001 |\n82\t| HLR-11 | P2 | Status message granularity: WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck pending/retry | E001 (engineering), E006 (wording) |\n83\t\n84\tFull coverage: all 11 HLRs map to at least one epic. E005 and E007 are support streams (design and documentation) and do not own HLRs; E005 enables the finalized visual treatment of HLR-3/HLR-4 and E006 owns the wording deliverable behind HLR-5/HLR-11's override table.\n85\t\n86\t**Priority-bundling decisions**:\n87\t- HLR-10 and HLR-11 (P2) are bundled into the P0 status-model epic E001 rather than split: HLR-10 (structured, state-driven derivation) is the foundation the P0 eviction/requeue/status HLRs build on — the Staff input's architecture constraints mandate state-driven derivation for exactly the P0 behaviors. HLR-11 distinguishes message states on the same override surface. All five HLRs share the same data structures (`WorkloadCondition` types, Workload CR conditions) and the same UI surface (workbench status display); splitting would force two epics to build the same status pipeline plus an artificial serialization edge.\n88\t- HLR-7/8/9 (all P1) share the HardwareProfile form/dropdown/popover surface — one epic, no deferrable split.\n89\t\n90\t## Health Warnings\n91\t\n92\t- **RBAC open question (non-blocking)**: Whether data scientists hold `view`/`edit`/`batch-user` bindings that aggregate Kueue's `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` is unresolved. Code handles 403 gracefully either way; if the role is absent, queue position is effectively admin-only. Tracked as a validation AC on E003 and owned by AI Core Platform (per the strategy's open-questions table), not as a DAG gate.\n93\t- **Placeholder-swap follow-up**: Placeholder visual treatment (E002) and default message copy (E001) ship ahead of RHOAIUX-7470 deliverables (E005/E006). Applying the finalized designs/copy is a small follow-on integration task on the dashboard; the engineering epics carry ACs ensuring the override table and indicator elements are structured so swap-in needs no rework. This is a schedule/coordination risk, not a missing scope item.\n94\t- **Pre-refinement content superseded**: The strategy's upper \"Proposed Solution\"/\"User Stories\" sections describe resource-quota columns, estimated wait times, and historical queue data. These are superseded by Staff input scope constraints (out of scope) and are intentionally not covered by any epic. Anyone reading the strategy top-down should use the HLR list as definitive.\n95\t- **Priority note**: E005/E006 are P1 despite serving P0 features' final polish — the strategy explicitly makes them non-blocking, so priority inheritance does not apply.\n96\t\n97\t## Tiered Delivery\n98\t\n99\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing gating user value: the only external-ish dependency (UXD/content via RHOAIUX-7470) is explicitly non-blocking, with placeholder-driven engineering as Tier-independent parallel work. All implementation epics deliver value independently.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-904dca4bc3aa6045","agent_id":"af23e71b7643ed18a","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"7c3e1b4c-8aa3-4813-8240-f6d0c70a5d4d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:09:08.862Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88ed4d66fc1c6eb6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
