{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-976d75668cc48b10","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Kueue management indicators: positive project indicator and non-Kueue workload\n4\t  anomaly indicator'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard UI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Kueue Management Indicators: Project Indicator and Workload Anomaly Indicator\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic adds two complementary UI indicators to the odh-dashboard that tell users whether their project and workbenches are managed by Kueue queue-based scheduling: a positive indicator on the project details page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, and an anomaly indicator on individual workloads that are NOT managed by Kueue despite living in a Kueue-managed namespace. Users must know their project uses queue-based scheduling because it fundamentally affects how their workloads start.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Add a positive Kueue indicator to the project details page, shown when the namespace carries the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label. The exact visual form (info banner, badge, or label) is a UX decision tracked as RHOAIUX-7470; implement an interim visual treatment so development is not blocked, structured so the finalized design can be applied without rework.\n39\t- Add an anomaly indicator on workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label — e.g. created via GitOps or CLI bypassing the dashboard). Do NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every workload in a Kueue-managed namespace — only flag the anomaly.\n40\t- Both indicators must be conditional on namespace/workload labels only; no new backend services or API changes.\n41\t- Indicator logic must not block workload creation or any dashboard workflow (read-only visibility).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists and absent when it does not.\n46\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n47\t- Given a namespace that is not Kueue-managed, when the user views the workbenches overview, then no workload shows the anomaly indicator regardless of queue labels, measured by the indicator being absent on all workloads in non-managed namespaces.\n48\t- Given the interim visual treatment, when the finalized design arrives from the UX stream (RHOAIUX-7470), then the treatment can be swapped without changing the indicator conditions or data plumbing, measured by the indicator presentation being isolated from its label-driven logic.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n53\t- HLR-4 [P0]: Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-904dca4bc3aa6045","agent_id":"af23e71b7643ed18a","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"8dd43584-e42e-4f8b-bd3a-5d85920fae31","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:09:13.342Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-976d75668cc48b10","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
