{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3273d0afd23322c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E006\n3\ttitle: Status message microcopy overrides for Kueue workload conditions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Content\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Status Message Microcopy Overrides for Kueue Workload Conditions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic authors the human-readable status message wording for Kueue workload conditions in the odh-dashboard: a microcopy override table mapping known condition/reason combinations to plain-language messages, reviewed under RHOAIUX-7470. Raw Kueue condition messages are unintelligible to data scientists; this content deliverable replaces engineering-authored defaults in the dashboard's data-driven override lookup table. Engineering is not blocked on this content — defaults ship first and are replaced when this epic delivers.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Author human-friendly override copy for the known Kueue condition/reason combinations, including at minimum: Preempted (higher-priority workload took resources), PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck (pending and retry states), ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded, Evicted (admin action or timeout), Requeued (with retry count and next retry time presentation), and the WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart distinction.\n38\t- Write copy suitable for data scientists and platform operators who are not Kubernetes-savvy, while remaining factually accurate about the underlying condition.\n39\t- Preserve the fallback rule in all copy decisions: when no override exists, the raw Kueue condition message is shown — copy never removes or masks the raw fallback.\n40\t- Deliver the overrides as a lookup table consumable by the dashboard's override mechanism (keyed by condition/reason combination), reviewed with UXD under RHOAIUX-7470.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given the enumerated set of known Kueue condition/reason combinations, when the content work completes, then every combination has reviewed human-readable copy, measured by a complete lookup table with one entry per known combination.\n45\t- Given a user without Kubernetes knowledge, when an override message is displayed, then the message explains the state in plain language without requiring Kueue concepts, measured by content review sign-off under RHOAIUX-7470.\n46\t- Given a condition/reason combination not covered by the table, when the dashboard renders it, then the raw Kueue condition message still displays, measured by the copy deliverable not altering the raw-message fallback behavior.\n47\t- Given the dashboard's data-driven override mechanism, when the reviewed copy is delivered, then it can be loaded without code changes, measured by the deliverable matching the lookup-table format the status model implementation consumes.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-11 [P2] (wording deliverable): Improve status message granularity — distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states. The engineering state derivation for this HLR lives in the status model implementation; this epic owns the wording.\n52\t- Supporting stream for HLR-5 [P0]: human-friendly message overrides for workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions (engineering defaults are replaced by this epic's reviewed copy).\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-904dca4bc3aa6045","agent_id":"af23e71b7643ed18a","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"d4f96540-2ae0-4c23-bb5a-36d686d6f820","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:09:19.135Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3273d0afd23322c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
