{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a94c1cb8d00a0901","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E005\n3\ttitle: UX design and content review for Kueue visibility indicators (RHOAIUX-7470)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: UXD\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# UX Design and Content Review for Kueue Visibility Indicators (RHOAIUX-7470)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the UX design decisions and visual treatments for the Kueue visibility features in the odh-dashboard, tracked as RHOAIUX-7470: the visual form of the positive Kueue indicator on the project details page, the design of the non-Kueue workload anomaly indicator, and the content review of status message wording. Engineering proceeds in parallel with placeholder treatments and default copy; this epic's deliverables replace them when finalized.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Decide and specify the visual form of the positive Kueue indicator on the project details page (info banner vs. badge vs. label), shown when a namespace carries the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label. The requirement is non-negotiable: users must know their project uses queue-based scheduling; the exact form is the open design decision this epic resolves.\n38\t- Design the anomaly indicator for workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are not Kueue-managed (missing queue label, e.g. GitOps/CLI-created), serving the hybrid GitOps + dashboard user.\n39\t- Review and finalize status message content in partnership with the content/microcopy stream: human-readable overrides for known Kueue condition/reason combinations (RHOAIUX-7470 content review).\n40\t- Deliver designs in a form the dashboard frontend can apply without rework (the engineering implementation isolates presentation from label-driven logic and keeps message overrides data-driven).\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given the project details page indicator requirement, when design work completes, then a finalized visual treatment specification is delivered for the positive Kueue indicator, measured by a design deliverable naming the chosen form (banner/badge/label) with usage guidance.\n45\t- Given the anomaly indicator requirement, when design work completes, then a visual treatment specification is delivered for the non-Kueue workload indicator, measured by a design deliverable defining the indicator's appearance and placement in the workbenches overview.\n46\t- Given the engineering defaults for status message overrides, when content review completes, then reviewed/finalized wording decisions are recorded for the known condition/reason combinations, measured by sign-off recorded against RHOAIUX-7470.\n47\t- Given the parallel engineering implementation using placeholders, when the finalized designs are delivered, then they are applicable without structural rework, measured by handoff artifacts referencing the implemented indicator elements and override table structure.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- Supporting stream (no HLR ownership): enables the finalized visual treatment for HLR-3 (positive Kueue indicator on project details page) and HLR-4 (anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads), and the content review behind the HLR-5 message overrides. Engineering implementations of those HLRs are not blocked on this epic — placeholder treatment and default copy are used until deliverables land.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3260fbd6f9eb2e","agent_id":"aa7f5869a08c0733a","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"0aa8228c-17a0-4254-8721-9caa2dd9e06d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:12:36.822Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a94c1cb8d00a0901","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
