ation, dropdown filtering explanation).\n45\t- Determine and record whether feature-level documentation beyond the release note is warranted, and deliver it if so.\n46\t- Cover user-facing behavioral notes: position data availability depends on the user's RBAC (silently omitted on 403); queue labels applied directly via GitOps are a supported pattern; missing LocalQueue warnings at workbench creation are non-blocking.\n47\t- Technically review all content against the implemented behavior before publication.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given the completed implementation work, when documentation is authored, then a release note covering all shipped Kueue visibility capabilities exists, measured by a published or publication-ready release note enumerating the features.\n52\t- Given the question of feature-level documentation, when the determination is made, then the decision and its rationale are recorded, measured by a documented go/no-go decision — with the documentation delivered if the decision is go.\n53\t- Given the documented behavior, when technical review runs, then all documented claims match the implemented behavior, measured by review sign-off against the shipped features.\n54\t- Given the RBAC-dependent queue position behavior, when the release note is written, then it states that queue position may not be visible to all users depending on permissions, measured by the caveat appearing in the published note.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- Supporting stream (no HLR ownership): documents the delivered capabilities behind HLR-1 through HLR-11. Documentation is blocked by all implementation work in this strategy per the docs-last rule.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3260fbd6f9eb2e","agent_id":"aa7f5869a08c0733a","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"f28befe3-7f18-4e51-af5d-94572748191f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:13:33.923Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc85adbddac6d5de","permiss