older treatment.\n42\t- Apply the finalized visual treatment for the non-Kueue workload anomaly indicator in the workbenches overview.\n43\t- Load the reviewed microcopy override table (known condition/reason combinations) into the dashboard's data-driven override mechanism, replacing engineering-authored defaults; no changes to status derivation logic.\n44\t- Verify the raw-message fallback behavior is unaffected by the copy swap (unknown conditions still display the raw Kueue condition message).\n45\t- Confirm the applied treatments and copy behave correctly across the states the placeholders covered (eviction reasons, requeued/retry state, AdmissionCheck pending/retry, WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given the finalized visual treatment specification for the positive Kueue indicator, when it is applied, then the project details page displays the chosen indicator form in place of the placeholder, measured by the rendered indicator matching the delivered specification when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists and the placeholder treatment no longer rendering.\n50\t- Given the finalized visual treatment specification for the anomaly indicator, when it is applied, then non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces display the finalized indicator, measured by the rendered indicator matching the delivered specification and appearing only on workloads missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label.\n51\t- Given the reviewed microcopy override table, when it is loaded, then every known condition/reason combination displays the reviewed wording, measured by the displayed status text matching the reviewed table entries and the swap-in diff containing no status-derivation logic changes.\n52\t- Given a condition/reason combination not covered by the reviewed table, when the dashboard renders it, then the raw Kueue condition message still displays, measured by the raw-message fallback behavior being unchanged after the copy swap.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Supporting stream (no HLR ownership): applies the finalized visual treatments for HLR-3 (positive Kueue indicator on project details page) and HLR-4 (anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads), and the reviewed wording behind the HLR-5/HLR-11 message override table. The engineering implementations of those HLRs complete independently and are not blocked on this epic's inputs; this epic replaces their placeholders with the finalized deliverables.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b90076d6a4b1a6ed","agent_id":"a7cd0b3b14fbc947b","session_id":"6e556f5d-8f87-4575-9eb4-8b9f55533407","uuid":"545eae8d-fe04-4d98-911c-943191f995a3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:19:01.988Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8923c833192b4fb7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised RHAISTRAT-8002"}
