ct. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set anywhere, and none are needed — the E005/E006 → E008 edges are true artifact-consumer dependencies, correctly expressed as `dependencies` only.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nAll 8 epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with `investigation_signals: null` — type-appropriate fields throughout. All 8 ai-signals rationale files exist and their values match frontmatter. Spot-checked consistency: E001 `open_questions: 1` is justified (all design decisions resolved by Staff input; pending UX copy is data content, non-approach-changing); E002 `open_questions: 0` is a defensible borderline (the open question affects its own deliverable's final form but not the approach, per the mandated interim treatment); E005/E006 `repo_access: 0` and `human_process_gates: -1` correctly reflect design/content deliverables with required review cycles; E008 `human_process_gates: 1` correctly avoids double-counting the review cycles charged to E005/E006. No signal value contradicts the rubric or the strategy content. (Arithmetic/thresholds not checked, per pipeline ownership.)\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable, measured-by acceptance criteria, and the strategy's 11 definitive ACs are all carried through. Rule-mandated ACs: E001 (replacement of the status model) carries the rollback-safety AC (unchanged behavior on non-Kueue fixtures); E007 (docs-authoring) carries the technical-review sign-off AC; no konflux chain exists. No non-testable external-schedule ACs found (E003's RBAC-validation AC is measured by a recorded finding — testable). No bare draft-ID references (\"E001\" etc.) in any epic body.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: 11/11 HLRs mapped, 11/11 definitive acceptance criteria present as epic ACs, all four NFRs covered (backwards compatibility and unknown-condition handling in E001 scope+ACs; 403 graceful degradation